# Shared content, COPIED into each consuming repo by the harness — git will not read an
# ignore file through a symlink. Edit it in the harness, not in a consuming repo: a local
# edit is overwritten on the next run, and comments here are not rescued.
#
# READ scripts/README.md IN THE HARNESS -> "The two copied files" BEFORE DELETING A LINE.
# This is the single place that ignores everything the agent tooling writes, so several
# shared commands assume these paths are uncommittable. Patterns a repo adds for itself go
# below the marker the refresh writes at the end.

# Both globs are needed — read the README before dropping either.
active-work-context/*
active-work-context/.*
!active-work-context/README.md
!active-work-context/.prettierrc.yml

sessions/

# Globbed, not listed — read the README before spelling these out.
*-status.log

hook-payloads/
.tmp/
localhistory/
handoffs/
handoff-log/
conversations/
hook-measurement/
